    "total_seconds": 7.240342535005766,
    "answer": "Under **Information Security Policy**, privileged administrator access must use least privilege and MFA, be assigned to an individual auditable account rather than a shared account, and be reviewed quarterly. Passwords must meet ACME\u2019s complexity, 90-day expiration, and reuse rules; remote data must use TLS 1.2 or higher, and the laptop must have full-disk encryption enabled.\n\nUnder **Acceptable Use Policy**, the administrator may not bypass the VPN, disable endpoint protection, store sensitive data on personal devices, or use personal email for business. Under **Remote Work Policy**, they must maintain a safe, distraction-free workspace and obtain prior written approval from HR and Legal before working outside their country of employment.",
